      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not directly related, but something I\u0027m not sure I thought about in the earlier review is that stdin has a limited buffer, and if the process doesn\u0027t read it then I suspect this will eventually fail and thus exit the script before the child process has finished, although it\u0027ll take a really long time and is quite unlikely to happen in practice. However, I wonder wouldn\u0027t it work just as well to not write anything at all here? Afaik there\u0027s no \"autoclosing\" of the standard fd\u0027s just because they\u0027re idle.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 60,
